WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.949
"The Benefits and Side Effects of Celery"

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.840
Some plants may help us
reduce high blood pressure

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.160
and celery may be one of them.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.560
But celery also contains relatively
high levels of sodium for a vegetable—

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.960
about 100 mg of sodium in one cup
(~130 g) of chopped celery.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.120
Even though it's relatively
high in sodium,

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:26.160
it also contains other compounds
like NBP,

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.240
the compound primarily responsible
for celery's taste and aroma,

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.920
which can relax
the smooth muscles

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.600
that line blood vessels,

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.640
potentially resulting
in lower blood pressure.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.320
And there are other
compounds in celery

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.120
that likely have
antihypertensive effects,

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.680
but those are all based
on rodent studies—

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:44.480
and indeed,

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.800
celery seed appears
to lower blood pressure

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.720
in hypertensive rats.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.080
But what about humans?

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:54.240
You don't know until you put
celery seed to the test,

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:57.280
or in this case,
celery seed extract,

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:59.840
in a randomized, triple-blind,
placebo-controlled,

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:02.000
cross-over, clinical trial.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.880
After four weeks of taking
the celery seed extract,

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:07.840
systolic blood pressure dropped
by at least 10 points

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.800
and diastolic blood pressure
by about 8 points.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.280
But the whole celery seed
equivalent would be way more

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:14.720
than people could eat.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.560
Is there anything a
more modest sprinkle

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:19.200
of celery seed a day
might help with?

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.160
Look at this:

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.000
"Treatment of women's
sexual dysfunction

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.360
using celery seed
(Apium graveolens):

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:24.800
A double-blind, randomized,

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:27.440
placebo-controlled
clinical trial."

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.360
And this study used
a culinary-friendly dose

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:32.320
of celery seed—
about 500 mg.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.800
That's about ¼ tsp per capsule,
three times per day.

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:38.160
At the end of six weeks,

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:39.440
there was
a significant improvement

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:41.440
in the self-reported
sexual functioning

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:45.120
among those eating celery seeds,
with significant improvements

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.800
across multiple measures
within just three weeks.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.800
What about celery juice?

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:52.160
There was a case
report of a man

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:54.400
who juiced a bunch
of celery every day

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.480
and had a drop
in blood pressure

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:59.040
and what appeared to be a
nonrandomized controlled trial

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:02.880
in which an undisclosed amount
of celery juice seemed to help.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.200
A review concluded
that celery can be considered

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.440
an antihypertensive agent,

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:10.160
but the quality of evidence
seems slight.

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:11.840
What's the downside though?

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:14.320
Well, celery seed
is generally considered safe,

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.080
and a safety evaluation
was performed

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:18.720
in the blood pressure trial
that indicated so,

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:21.120
but maybe not for everybody.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:23.040
Here is a case report
of someone who had been taking

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.320
about two tablespoons
of dried celery leaves a day,

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:29.520
and it seemed to cause overactive
thyroid gland activity;

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.440
the same happened
to this woman,

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:35.200
who had been taking celery
extract powder for weight loss.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:39.040
She did lose 57 pounds (26 kg)
in 78 days

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:41.360
but that was likely because
the celery extract

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.360
led to hyperthyroidism.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.280
That is not a healthy way
to lose weight,

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:49.760
risking side effects with names
like thyrotoxic paralysis.

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:52.480
Celery is also
an allergen for some,

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:55.520
often called
"pollen-related food allergy."

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:57.520
People who are allergic
to some pollens

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:00.320
are more likely to have
an allergy to celery,

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:02.000
such as what happened
in this rare case

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.840
of severe anaphylactic shock

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:07.120
after consumption
of raw celery.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.360
Some only get allergic reactions
to celery

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:12.160
if they eat it
before exercising.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:14.960
Heating celery eradicates
symptoms for about 50 percent

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:18.400
of people with a celery allergy,
but those who react

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:21.920
to raw celery also react
when it's dried.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:24.160
Even if you don't have
a celery allergy,

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:26.720
a warning for those
who eat a lot of celery,

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:31.360
celery juice, or celeriac,
also known as celery root.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:33.440
There are compounds
called psoralens

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:35.600
in the celery/parsnip/
parsley family

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:38.320
that can make you
sensitive to sunlight.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.000
Farmworkers can suffer
from a condition

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.520
known as celery blisters,

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:45.600
when handling plants without
skin protection in the sun.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.400
Even grocery store workers
who go from the produce aisle

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:51.200
to the tanning salon
can get into trouble.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.440
These compounds can make
their way into our skin

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:55.360
from the inside out as well,

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:58.080
and they are not
destroyed by cooking.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:01.440
Too much time in the sun after
commencing a "celery soup diet"

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:02.960
or spending time
on a tanning bed

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:06.080
an hour after eating
just one large celery root

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:10.765
may be enough to result
in a serious blistering burn.

